          "guid": "mrx6cmyicaiuh2cm",
          "message": {
            "text": "Attach resolution hooks in at `pickAiCommand` (after the on-PATH check, before returning the bare binary) rather than a codex-specific launch route, so it applies to EVERY `{{aiCommand}}`/`{{claudeCommand}}` codex expansion — the default AI terminal, custom terminal templates, and worker-worktree terminals. Worker worktrees get the right semantics for free: each worktree's own `dataDir` → its own `codex-app-server.json` → attach to its own driven thread. The fallback when `codexTerminalAttachCommand` returns null is the plain `codex` binary (pre-HS-9394 behavior), deliberately NOT a fresh `codex --remote` daemon session — that would be daemon-attached but still not the driven thread, adding daemon-dependence without watch value (docs/123 §123.5). See also `src/codexAppServer.ts` (the condition set).\n",
            "markdown": "Attach resolution hooks in at `pickAiCommand` (after the on-PATH check, before returning the bare binary) rather than a codex-specific launch route, so it applies to EVERY `{{aiCommand}}`/`{{claudeCommand}}` codex expansion — the default AI terminal, custom terminal templates, and worker-worktree terminals. Worker worktrees get the right semantics for free: each worktree's own `dataDir` → its own `codex-app-server.json` → attach to its own driven thread. The fallback when `codexTerminalAttachCommand` returns null is the plain `codex` binary (pre-HS-9394 behavior), deliberately NOT a fresh `codex --remote` daemon session — that would be daemon-attached but still not the driven thread, adding daemon-dependence without watch value (docs/123 §123.5). See also `src/codexAppServer.ts` (the condition set).\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/terminals/resolveCommand.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 149,
                  "endLine": 156,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  if (tool === 'codex') {\n    const attach = (options.codexAttachOverride ?? codexTerminalAttachCommand)(options.dataDir);\n    if (attach !== null) return attach;\n  }\n  return bin;\n}\n\n/** Read the project's `ai_tool` setting (default `auto` when absent). */"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
